# Single source of truth for pinned build/codegen tool versions.
#
# Consumers:
#   - .devcontainer/Dockerfile: the `just dev-image` target (see justfile)
#     reads this file and passes every entry through as `docker build
#     --build-arg KEY=VALUE`. The Dockerfile's ARGs have NO defaults on
#     purpose (see the Dockerfile's guard RUN) — a default would recreate a
#     second source of truth that could silently disagree with this file.
#   - .github/workflows/release-completer.yml: runs in goreleaser-cross, not
#     the devcontainer image, so it cannot just inherit these — it loads this
#     same file into $GITHUB_ENV and installs buf/protoc-gen-go/
#     protoc-gen-go-grpc/versionator at the versions named here.
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml: the build-container job builds
#     .devcontainer/Dockerfile directly via docker/build-push-action (not
#     `just dev-image`), so it loads this file into a step output and passes
#     it as that action's `build-args` input. It does that through
#     `just tool-version-args` (build/ci.justfile), which is also what
#     release-completer.yml's `just release-install-tools` sources.
#   - .github/actions/setup-just: every workflow step is a `just` target, so
#     runners outside the devcontainer image have to install `just` before
#     they can run one. It reads JUST_VERSION here so a runner and the image
#     can never disagree about which `just` is running the CI contract.
#   - .github/workflows/ci.yml's windows job: it cannot run the Linux
#     devcontainer image, so it installs Go itself, at GO_VERSION here, via
#     `just ci-go-version` (build/ci.justfile).
#   - justfile's gitleaks-install: lefthook's pre-commit secret scan runs on
#     the host, so it installs gitleaks there at GITLEAKS_VERSION here.
#   - justfile's shfmt-install: `just fmt` and lefthook's pre-commit shell
#     formatter run shfmt on the host, so it installs shfmt there at
#     SHFMT_VERSION here.
#
# internal/shared/buildpins' drift-gate tests parse this file
# plus the Dockerfile and both workflows and fail if any of them disagree,
# or if a consumer stops deriving from this file altogether.
#
# Checksum pins, <TOOL>_SHA256_<ARCH>, are the sha256 of the download
# <TOOL>_VERSION names, one per TARGETARCH the image builds for; the Dockerfile
# verifies the download against them before extracting it. They move with
# their version: scripts/lint-pins refuses a version bump that leaves one
# behind, and a checksum change under an unchanged version. Take the values
# from the upstream's published list, never from hashing a download:
#   Go:   https://go.dev/dl/?mode=json&include=all, the `sha256` of the linux
#         `archive` files.
#   just: https://github.com/casey/just/releases/download/<ver>/SHA256SUMS, the
#         lines for just-<ver>-{x86_64,aarch64}-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz
#         (AMD64, ARM64), just-<ver>-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz (DARWINARM64)
#         and just-<ver>-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip (WINDOWSAMD64).
#
# An <ARCH> that is not one the image builds for (DARWINARM64, WINDOWSAMD64)
# pins a CI runner's download, not the image's: .github/actions/setup-just
# reads it on the macOS and Windows runners, and no Dockerfile ARG or
# devcontainer.json build arg carries it. The arch suffix has no `_` in it, so
# scripts/lint-pins still pairs it with <TOOL>_VERSION.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, one per line, `#` comment lines and blank lines
# allowed — every consumer filters those out with `grep -v '^#' | grep -v
# '^$'` before treating the rest as KEY=VALUE pairs (so the same one-liner
# works whether the target is a GitHub Actions env file, a build-arg list, or
# a shell `source`). Do not add quoting or export statements; keep it boring.

GO_VERSION=1.26.9
GO_SHA256_AMD64=42d158b4d8f7b61ac0a830567c940a86098fb7aac52e467a5ebec03ef5cc2f8d
GO_SHA256_ARM64=4a97373d49fcacdcf3694fea368a500b00ee3e963974f3e7514132717632f052
UPX_VERSION=4.2.4
ONNX_VERSION=1.20.1
GOLANGCI_LINT_VERSION=2.12.1
BUF_VERSION=1.47.2
PROTOC_GEN_GO_VERSION=1.36.11
PROTOC_GEN_GO_GRPC_VERSION=1.6.2
GOMUTANTS_VERSION=0.7.0
VERSIONATOR_VERSION=0.2.3
GORELEASER_VERSION=2.16.0
# A git REVISION, not a version: reprise has published no release yet, so the
# image builds it from this full commit SHA of a PUSHED ref on
# github.com/ctxloom/reprise (the Dockerfile's reprise stage says why the image
# needs it). Replaced by REPRISE_VERSION and the release asset once reprise
# publishes v0.1.0. A SHA has no direction, so scripts/lint-pins refuses any
# change to it until the pin is named in CTXLOOM_ALLOW_PIN_DOWNGRADE.
REPRISE_REVISION=95a69cff0d5b3623607cef888542e50e2f02adaf
LIZARD_VERSION=1.22.2
JUST_VERSION=1.40.0
JUST_SHA256_AMD64=181b91d0ceebe8a57723fb648ed2ce1a44d849438ce2e658339df4f8db5f1263
JUST_SHA256_ARM64=d065d0df1a1f99529869fba8a5b3e0a25c1795b9007099b00dfabe29c7c1f7b6
JUST_SHA256_DARWINARM64=0fb2401a46409bdf574f42f92df0418934166032ec2bcb0fc7919b7664fdcc01
JUST_SHA256_WINDOWSAMD64=50d7c9b3ef3e38169bb62020cf8b091ac55e989c862fb0dde8af5a9b2505526a
GOPLS_VERSION=0.21.0
SERENA_AGENT_VERSION=2.0.0
GITLEAKS_VERSION=8.30.1
SHFMT_VERSION=3.14.1
LEFTHOOK_VERSION=1.13.6
GOVULNCHECK_VERSION=1.8.0
# Node.js, an LTS line: the Dockerfile's node RUN says why the image has it.
NODE_VERSION=24.21.0
# A floor, not a pin: the Dockerfile's git RUN says why.
GIT_MIN_VERSION=2.48.0
